{
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "Complete simulated land across Europe, Africa, Asia-Pacific and Greenland while deliberately leaving the Americas and Caribbean for a later expansion. Modern administrative boundaries are source geometry only; gameplay regions are regrouped into persistent physical zones.",
  "targetContinents": ["Europe", "Africa", "Asia", "Oceania"],
  "minimumSourceAreaSqKm": 8,
  "principles": [
    "Existing Sim-World regions always win and are never replaced by coarser source geometry.",
    "Modern borders are source geometry, not gameplay borders.",
    "Cluster source units across modern frontiers inside durable physical zones.",
    "Prefer basins, highlands, plateaus, coasts, steppe belts, deserts, mountain systems and island groups.",
    "Leave continental North America, South America and the Caribbean absent; include Greenland and the Pacific island world.",
    "Keep enough regional detail for Silk Road, monsoon, steppe, Indian Ocean and Pacific systems without reproducing every modern district."
